(>> Solution to Question 1:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the core methodology of 'Neutral User Testing'. Detail why testing facilitators must strictly adhere to the 'Show, Don't Tell' approach, and outline five critical behavioral rules to avoid biasing participants.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Epistemological Foundations of Neutral User Testing:) Tj
T*
(   - The primary objective of user testing is not to demonstrate that the software functions, but) Tj
T*
(   to uncover where human mental models clash with system reality.) Tj
T*
(   - Humans are acutely sensitive to authority and eager to please researchers \(Acquiescence Bias) Tj
T*
(   / Demand Characteristics\). Facilitator neutrality is mandatory to preserve experimental) Tj
T*
(   validity.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The 'Show, Don't Tell' Imperative:) Tj
T*
(   - In production, designers and engineers will not stand behind customers explaining what icons) Tj
T*
(   mean or apologizing for slow response times.) Tj
T*
(   - Placing the prototype in user hands without explanation forces the interface to stand on its) Tj
T*
(   own affordances, signifiers, and feedback loops. If the user cannot understand it unassisted,) Tj
T*
(   the design has failed.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Five Critical Behavioral Rules for Facilitators:) Tj
T*
(   - Rule 1: Never Answer Functional Inquiries Directly: When a participant asks: 'What happens if) Tj
T*
(   I click this?', reflect it neutrally: 'What do you expect would happen if you clicked that?') Tj
T*
(   - Rule 2: Maintain Completely Neutral Non-Verbal Demeanor: Refrain from nodding vigorously,) Tj
T*
(   smiling, gasping, or leaning forward when users approach the correct or incorrect controls.) Tj
T*
(   - Rule 3: Avoid Praise or Reassurance: Replace 'Good job!' or 'You got it right!' with) Tj
T*
(   objective acknowledgments: 'I see what you did; please keep narrating your thoughts.') Tj
T*
(   - Rule 4: Probe Hesitations Neutrally: When a user pauses for 10 seconds staring at a screen,) Tj
T*
(   gently ask: 'Tell me what you are looking at right now.') Tj
T*
(   - Rule 5: De-Personalize the Test Upfront: Explicitly inform the user: 'We are testing the) Tj
T*
(   prototype, NOT you. You cannot do anything wrong here. If something is confusing, it is) Tj
T*
(   entirely the fault of the design.') Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 2:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Deconstruct the 'Feedback Capture Matrix' \(Likes, Deltas, Questions, Ideas\). Illustrate how a design team uses this synthesis tool to process 20 hours of raw usability video footage into prioritized engineering backlogs.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Structural Architecture of the Feedback Capture Matrix:) Tj
T*
(   - Quadrant 1: Likes / Plus \(+\) [Upper-Left]: What worked well? Features, micro-interactions,) Tj
T*
(   copy, and flows that users praised, understood effortlessly, or expressed enthusiasm for.) Tj
T*
(   - Quadrant 2: Deltas / Criticisms \(^\) [Upper-Right]: What should be changed? Concrete friction) Tj
T*
(   points, errors, navigation bottlenecks, confusing terminology, and user complaints.) Tj
T*
(   - Quadrant 3: Questions \(?\) [Lower-Left]: What was ambiguous? Unanswered queries,) Tj
T*
(   uncertainties, and gaps in mental models raised by users \('Is this data shared with my boss?'\).) Tj
T*
(   - Quadrant 4: Ideas / Lightbulbs \(!\) [Lower-Right]: What new possibilities emerged? Unexpected) Tj
T*
(   use-cases, feature extensions, and creative workarounds spontaneously suggested by) Tj
T*
(   participants.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Synthesis Pipeline from 20 Hours of Video Footage:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1: Distributed Video Tagging: Cross-functional pairs \(engineer + UX designer\) review) Tj
T*
(   video footage, transcribing discrete observations onto physical or digital post-it notes coded) Tj
T*
(   with participant timestamps.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2: Live Collaborative Wall Sorting: The team sorts hundreds of notes into the four) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
