(>> Solution to Question 5:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Deconstruct Nielsen's Third Heuristic: 'User Control and Freedom' \(Emergency Exits\). Detail how providing non-destructive 'Undo' mechanics transforms user cognitive confidence in complex creative applications \(e.g., Photoshop, Figma\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Psychological Architecture of User Control and Freedom:) Tj
T*
(   - Users frequently choose software functions by mistake or experiment playfully with unfamiliar) Tj
T*
(   configurations.) Tj
T*
(   - If an accidental action leads to permanent, irreversible data destruction or traps the user) Tj
T*
(   in an inescapable modal labyrinth, the user experiences intense anxiety, cognitive paralysis,) Tj
T*
(   and risk-aversion.) Tj
T*
(   - Software must provide prominent, easily accessible 'Emergency Exits' \(Undo, Redo, Cancel,) Tj
T*
(   Reset\) that allow users to leave unwanted states effortlessly.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The Universal Power of the Multi-Level Undo \(Command+Z\):) Tj
T*
(   - In creative applications like Figma or Photoshop, users execute thousands of micro-decisions) Tj
T*
(   \(drawing bezier vectors, shifting color hues, transforming pixel layers\).) Tj
T*
(   - The Command Pattern Architecture: By implementing a robust historical state stack \(Gang of) Tj
T*
(   Four Command Pattern\) where every action encapsulates its own inverse operation, users can step) Tj
T*
(   backward and forward through infinite historical states.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Impact on Human Learning & Innovation:) Tj
T*
(   - When an interface guarantees that no action is permanently fatal, users explore wild,) Tj
T*
(   creative, and risky design alternatives with joyful confidence.) Tj
T*
(   - The fear of 'breaking the computer' drops to zero, accelerating software mastery and creative) Tj
T*
(   fluency.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 6:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Evaluate Nielsen's Fourth Heuristic: 'Consistency and Standards'. Contrast 'Internal Consistency' with 'External Consistency' using mobile navigation design patterns.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Foundations of Consistency:) Tj
T*
(   - Jakob's Law of Internet User Experience: 'Users spend most of their time on other websites.') Tj
T*
(   This means users bring established mental models from the rest of the digital world to your) Tj
T*
(   product.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Internal vs. External Consistency:) Tj
T*
(   - Internal Consistency:) Tj
T*
(   * Definition: Maintaining identical visual styling, typographic scale, button nomenclature, and) Tj
T*
(   interaction mechanics across all screens, tabs, and sub-systems within the same product suite.) Tj
T*
ET

