(   * Violation Example: If the primary confirmation button is styled with blue background on) Tj
T*
(   Screen A, but green on Screen B, and gray on Screen C, the user must expend cognitive working) Tj
T*
(   memory verifying button identity on every single screen.) Tj
T*
(   - External Consistency:) Tj
T*
(   * Definition: Adhering to platform-wide operating system conventions and global industry) Tj
T*
(   standards \(Apple Human Interface Guidelines, Google Material Design\).) Tj
T*
(   * Violation Example: An iOS app that designs a custom back button placed at the bottom-right) Tj
T*
(   corner of the screen, or overrides the standard swipe-from-left-edge back gesture, violently) Tj
T*
(   disrupts muscle memory established across millions of other iOS apps.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Engineering Optimization:) Tj
T*
(   - Universal design tokens and component libraries enforce internal consistency; adhering to) Tj
T*
(   native platform SDK guidelines guarantees external consistency.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
