BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 7:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Detail Nielsen's Fifth Heuristic: 'Error Prevention'. Categorize human errors into 'Slips' versus 'Mistakes' \(Don Norman\) and engineer specific UI safeguards against both.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Norman's Taxonomy of Human Errors:) Tj
T*
(   - Slips \(Execution Failures\): The user possesses the correct goal and mental model, but) Tj
T*
(   inadvertently executes the wrong physical action due to inattention, distraction, or fatigue) Tj
T*
(   \(e.g., intending to click 'Save', but accidentally clicking 'Delete' because the buttons were) Tj
T*
(   adjacent\).) Tj
T*
(   - Mistakes \(Knowledge/Planning Failures\): The user executes the action they intended, but their) Tj
T*
(   underlying goal or mental model was incorrect due to misunderstanding system rules \(e.g.,) Tj
T*
(   booking a flight for June 12th instead of July 12th because date formats were ambiguous\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Engineering Safeguards Against Slips:) Tj
T*
(   - Spatial Separation & Visual Asymmetry: Keep destructive actions far away from common actions) Tj
T*
(   \(place 'Delete Account' at the bottom of the page in red outline, isolated from 'Save) Tj
T*
(   Changes'\).) Tj
T*
(   - Confirmation Friction for Destructive Tasks: For permanent operations \(deleting a production) Tj
T*
(   database cluster\), require the user to explicitly type the exact name of the cluster) Tj
T*
(   \(`production-db-alpha`\) into a text box before enabling the delete button.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Engineering Safeguards Against Mistakes:) Tj
T*
(   - Helpful Constraints & Sensible Defaults: When a user selects a flight departure date,) Tj
T*
(   automatically disable and gray out all preceding calendar dates for the return flight.) Tj
T*
(   - Inline Real-Time Formatting Validation: Mask phone numbers and credit card fields) Tj
T*
(   automatically with spaces \(`\(555\) 123-4567`\), preventing formatting syntax errors before) Tj
T*
(   submission.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 8:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze Nielsen's Sixth Heuristic: 'Recognition Rather than Recall'. How does human working memory architecture explain why dropdown autocomplete search bars are superior to blank text input fields?) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Neurobiology of Human Memory Retrieval:) Tj
T*
(   - Human memory relies on two fundamentally different retrieval mechanisms:) Tj
T*
(   * Recall: The cognitive task of retrieving an informational item from long-term memory without) Tj
T*
(   any external sensory cues \(e.g., answering 'What is the exact terminal command to compress a) Tj
T*
(   directory with tar?'\). Recall requires high cognitive effort and exhaustive search across) Tj
T*
(   neural associative networks.) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
endobj
