(   2. Five Structural Qualities of Actionable Documentation:) Tj
T*
(   - Quality 1: Easy to Search with Natural Language: The documentation engine must support robust) Tj
T*
(   semantic search that maps user intent and misspellings to technical articles, rather than) Tj
T*
(   requiring exact keyword matching.) Tj
T*
(   - Quality 2: Focused on the User's Real Task: Organized around user jobs-to-be-done \('How to) Tj
T*
(   configure automated daily database backups'\) rather than internal architecture diagrams) Tj
T*
(   \('BackupDaemon Architecture'\).) Tj
T*
(   - Quality 3: Concrete, Numbered Step-by-Step Instructions: Clear sequential procedures \(Step 1,) Tj
T*
(   Step 2, Step 3\) with zero ambiguous narrative filler.) Tj
T*
(   - Quality 4: Runnable Code Snippets with Copy Buttons: Providing verified, syntax-highlighted) Tj
T*
(   code examples that developers can copy and paste with a single click, annotated with expected) Tj
T*
(   terminal output.) Tj
T*
(   - Quality 5: Contextual Progressive Disclosure: Embedding contextual tooltips and) Tj
T*
(   micro-documentation links directly inside the application UI right beside the complex control,) Tj
T*
(   so users never have to leave their workflow.) Tj
T*
