12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Deconstruct the four foundational principles of web accessibility \(WCAG 2.1 POUR: Perceivable, Operable, Understandable, Robust\). Provide concrete code-level examples of compliance for each.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Perceivable:) Tj
T*
(   - Principle: Information and UI components must be presentable to users in ways they can) Tj
T*
(   perceive \(cannot be invisible to all senses\).) Tj
T*
(   - Code Compliance: Non-text content must have text alternatives:) Tj
T*
(   `<img src='revenue_chart.png' alt='Bar chart showing Q3 revenue growth of 18% over Q2'>`) Tj
T*
(   - High Contrast Compliance: Text and background color meet minimum 4.5:1 ratio:) Tj
T*
(   `color: #212121; background-color: #FFFFFF; /* Contrast Ratio: 16.1:1 */`) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Operable:) Tj
T*
(   - Principle: Interface components and navigation must be operable via diverse input modalities.) Tj
T*
(   - Code Compliance: Full keyboard operability with visible focus indicators:) Tj
T*
(   `<button class='btn-primary' tabindex='0'>Deploy Cluster</button>`) Tj
T*
(   `button:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid #1A73E8; outline-offset: 2px; }`) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Understandable:) Tj
T*
(   - Principle: Information and operation of UI must be clear and predictable.) Tj
T*
(   - Code Compliance: Declare language attribute on root document and explicit form labels:) Tj
T*
(   `<html lang='en'>`) Tj
T*
(   `<label for='user-email'>Corporate Email Address</label>`) Tj
T*
(   `<input type='email' id='user-email' name='email' required aria-describedby='email-help'>`) Tj
T*
(   `<span id='email-help'>Format: name@company.com</span>`) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Robust:) Tj
T*
(   - Principle: Content must be reliably interpreted across diverse user agents and assistive) Tj
T*
(   technologies.) Tj
T*
(   - Code Compliance: Valid semantic HTML5 and proper ARIA states:) Tj
T*
(   `<nav aria-label='Main Navigation'>`) Tj
T*
(   `<button aria-expanded='false' aria-controls='menu-list'>Menu</button>`) Tj
T*
(   `<ul id='menu-list' hidden>...</ul>`) Tj
T*
(   `</nav>`) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 15:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the role of 'Task Scenarios' in usability testing. Contrast an effective 'Goal-Directed Scenario' with an ineffective 'Prescriptive Script' for testing an online banking wireframe.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Science of Usability Task Scenarios:) Tj
T*
(   - Scenarios provide participants with realistic context, authentic motivation, and an explicit) Tj
T*
(   objective, leaving them completely free to discover and navigate the path independently.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Ineffective Prescriptive Script \(What NOT to do\):) Tj
T*
(   - Script: 'Click on the blue 'Transfers' tab at the top. Select 'Wire Transfer' from the) Tj
T*
(   dropdown. Enter $500 in the amount field. Type account number 987654321. Click the green) Tj
T*
(   'Confirm' button at the bottom right.') Tj
T*
(   - Critique: This does not test usability, discoverability, or user mental models! It tests) Tj
T*
(   whether the participant is capable of following robotic reading commands. Yields zero) Tj
T*
(   actionable design data.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Effective Goal-Directed Scenario \(The Gold Standard\):) Tj
T*
