BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the 'Single Ease Question' \(SEQ\) methodology. How does administering a 1-item 7-point post-task question provide high-sensitivity diagnostics across iterative usability sprints?) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Architecture of the Single Ease Question \(Jeff Sauro\):) Tj
T*
(   - Administered immediately after a participant finishes \(or fails\) a single discrete task) Tj
T*
(   scenario during usability testing.) Tj
T*
(   - Format: A standardized 7-point Likert scale:) Tj
T*
(   'Overall, how easy or difficult was it to complete this task?') Tj
T*
(   [1: Very Difficult | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5 | 6 | 7: Very Easy]) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Methodological & Psychometric Superiority:) Tj
T*
(   - High Sensitivity: Captures the raw, immediate cognitive friction while the task experience is) Tj
T*
(   completely fresh in working memory, before memory decay or halo effects from subsequent tasks) Tj
T*
(   blur perception.) Tj
T*
(   - Low Administrative Overhead: Takes 5 seconds to answer, preventing survey fatigue across 10) Tj
T*
(   multi-step scenarios.) Tj
T*
(   - Benchmark Standards: Across thousands of industry software tasks, the empirical historical) Tj
T*
(   average SEQ score is 5.5. A task scoring below 5.0 signals severe operational friction) Tj
T*
(   requiring immediate redesign.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Diagnostic Triangulation:) Tj
T*
(   - Cross-referencing SEQ with Task Completion Rate reveals critical insights:) Tj
T*
(   * High Completion + Low SEQ: Users eventually completed the task, but found it agonizingly) Tj
T*
(   painful and complex.) Tj
T*
(   * Low Completion + High SEQ: The dangerous 'Blind Failure' mode?users thought the task was easy) Tj
T*
(   because they executed the wrong operation and never realized they failed!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
