T*
(   2. Modal Dialog Accessible Focus Loop Protocol:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1: Trapping Focus on Open:) Tj
T*
(   * When the modal opens, save the trigger button reference \(`document.activeElement`\).) Tj
T*
(   * Set programmatic focus immediately to the first interactive element inside the modal or the) Tj
T*
(   modal heading: `modalRef.focus\(\)`.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2: Cyclic Tab Constraint:) Tj
T*
(   * Add a keyboard event listener \(`KeyDown`\). If the user presses `Tab` on the last interactive) Tj
T*
(   element inside the modal, cycle focus back to the first interactive element. If `Shift+Tab` on) Tj
T*
(   the first element, cycle to the last.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3: Background Inactivation:) Tj
T*
(   * Apply `aria-modal='true'` and `aria-hidden='true'` \(or native `inert` attribute\) to the) Tj
T*
(   background application container so screen readers cannot navigate into obscured content.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 4: Restoring Focus on Close:) Tj
T*
(   * When the user presses `Esc` or clicks 'Close', destroy the modal and programmatically return) Tj
T*
(   focus to the original trigger button, allowing the user to seamlessly resume their workflow.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
