12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Evaluate the 'Hawkeye Missile Alert' false alarm in Hawaii \(2018\) as a case study in usability engineering failure. Propose three concrete architectural UI countermeasures.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Hawaii Missile Crisis \(January 13, 2018\):) Tj
T*
(   - At 8:07 AM, the Hawaii Emergency Management Agency transmitted a terrifying live alert to) Tj
T*
(   millions of smartphones: 'BALLISTIC MISSILE THREAT INBOUND TO HAWAII. SEEK IMMEDIATE SHELTER.) Tj
T*
(   THIS IS NOT A DRILL.') Tj
T*
(   - 38 minutes of statewide terror and panic ensued before a retraction was broadcast.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Root Usability Engineering Flaws:) Tj
T*
(   - Heuristic 5 \(Error Prevention Failure\): The software dashboard presented a dense, plain-text) Tj
T*
(   dropdown menu where the live nuclear alert option \(`PACOM \(CDW\) - STATE ONLY`\) was listed) Tj
T*
(   immediately adjacent to the routine daily test drill option \(`DRILL - PACOM \(CDW\) - STATE) Tj
T*
(   ONLY`\). Both options shared identical font sizes and styling.) Tj
T*
(   - Missing Confirmation Context: The confirmation dialog merely asked: 'Are you sure you want to) Tj
T*
(   proceed?', without explicitly displaying the exact text of the alert or distinguishing drills) Tj
T*
(   from real attacks.) Tj
T*
(   - Heuristic 9 \(Recovery Failure\): The software lacked an automated retraction broadcast) Tj
T*
(   template.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Three Concrete Architectural Countermeasures:) Tj
T*
(   - Countermeasure 1: Structural Spatial & Visual Segregation:) Tj
T*
(   * Completely isolate drill operations from live emergency broadcasts. Place live alerts inside) Tj
T*
(   an encrypted red modal requiring physical keycard swipe or dual-operator authorization.) Tj
T*
(   - Countermeasure 2: Explicit Verbatim Preview Confirmation:) Tj
T*
(   * The confirmation modal must render the exact SMS text that will appear on citizens' phones,) Tj
T*
(   requiring the operator to manually type the word 'BROADCAST' before sending.) Tj
T*
(   - Countermeasure 3: One-Click Automated Emergency Retraction:) Tj
T*
(   * Pre-program an automated 'Cancel / False Alarm' broadcast button that instantly fires) Tj
T*
(   retraction alerts across cellular networks with zero manual phone calls.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
